## CX-P3 self vacuity read — second reader still REQUIRED
All names below are in Nanodregg.Lang.Contextual.Worlds (last nine under Experiment). This is the author's read, not CHARTER law 6's second-agent approval. DISJUNCT CHECK: none of the 21 theorem conclusions has an Or branch that can discharge the claim independently. Iff claims are read in both directions; conjunctions are all required. No unbounded existential collision predicate is introduced. Price premises: none.

1. derives_head: actual reduct derivation implies membership in original program heads. This is a structural support lemma, not an admission claim. A body-only atom cannot satisfy the premise; an enabled empty-body rule makes it inhabited. No conclusion disjunct or existential.
2. closed_complete: closed finite iterate plus independent Derives entails computed membership. Closure alone does not imply arbitrary membership; derivability alone does not imply membership at insufficient fuel. Empty-body facts and positive chains inhabit the premises. No conclusion disjunct.
3. check_iff_stable: saturation relates a concrete Bool check to the independent inductive least-model statement. Saturation alone proves neither acceptance nor stability (the two-rule union is saturated and rejected). Both directions use grounded soundness/completeness; not P iff P.
4. check_decides: a completed result some b determines stability exactly when b=true. The premise does not assert b=true; union gives a real false branch. It does not turn none into false. No conclusion disjunct.
5. unfounded_excluded: accepted world, an unfounded-set condition on its reduct, and x in that set imply x absent. The set cannot be empty because hx supplies a member. An enabled empty-body rule for x defeats hr, so it cannot refute grounded facts. Uses landed unfounded_not_derivable; no vacuous fallback.
6. collect_checked: completed collection implies every INPUT world had a completed Boolean check, including rejected worlds. Witness b is Bool and the check equation is load-bearing; Option may otherwise be none. Empty input is the structural base, not the only inhabited instance.
7. collect_mem: returned membership iff input membership AND accepted check. Neither condition alone suffices; the union is an input but rejected, and accepted worlds outside an explicitly supplied input are not returned. No conclusion disjunct; both iff directions read.
8. analyze_exact: output membership iff enumerated input AND independent Stable. Completed analysis may contain both successes and failures among inputs. Neither stable status nor enumeration alone implies the complete conjunction.
9. mem_subsets_iff: computed powerset membership iff structural Sublist. Both sides vary with v/xs; [1] is enumerated under [0,1], [2] is not. This is coverage of enumeration, not merely a membership projection.
10. analyze_sublist_exact: consumer-facing form of analyze_exact using the independently proved enumeration coverage. Canonical sublist premise is explicit, with stability still necessary. Deliberate corollary, no new semantic premise on anything landed.
11. alternatives_sound: a computed alternatives report entails two Stable worlds, positive evidence in one, negative evidence in the other, and unequal worlds. The constructor accepts arbitrary lists at the type level; report must establish these facts through checking and enumeration. Incompatibility of the query atoms is a caller interpretation, not an inferred theorem about arbitrary Nat labels. All five conjuncts required.
12. noJustification_sound: witness ws is the actual completed finite analysis result; ws is nonempty and neither query atom occurs in any member. The nonempty conjunct prevents vacuity from an inconsistent program with zero worlds. The two-rule program with both supports withdrawn supplies ws=[[]], an inhabited premise.
13. Experiment.two_rule_worlds: concrete computation yields the EXACT two worlds and checks both separately. No premise; all three conjuncts checked by decide, no disjunct hiding failure. Default/grounding/reverse-inclusion mutations refute it.
14. admissible_not_union_closed: both singleton worlds accepted AND their union rejected. Both operands are explicitly named, no unbounded witness. The rejection conjunct is the substance; the operand acceptance conjuncts prevent a non-world operand from faking non-closure.
15. union_not_stable: exact same union fails the independent Stable predicate, through check_decides. A real negative semantic claim, not merely negation of a check defined as Stable. No disjunct.
16. withdraw_and_reassert: one actual session, with retained rules and immutable token edits, computes all five exact world sets. No existentially chosen session and no optional branch. Restoring one/both tokens has distinct outputs.
17. reissue_does_not_restore_rule: old rule stays disabled while the new token is live and the old token dead. These are three required conjuncts; new-token liveness prevents an all-dead-world explanation. Existing reissue_never_reenables is unchanged.
18. four_reports: four computed reports at explicit inputs, each a distinct constructor, checked by decide. Not an Or between tags and not an assertion that hand-constructed tags are different. Disabling completion falsifies the fourth; merging alternatives falsifies the second/third separation.
19. no_world_is_distinct: odd default loop gives noWorld; withdrawn program gives noJustification with an empty admissible world; one remaining rule gives supported. Three required outputs, preventing no-model/unknown/unsupported collapse.
20. cycle_loses_grounding_over_worlds: exact unique-world session before/withdraw/restore AND rejection of the old cycle world after withdrawal. Fact 5 and consequence 6 survive, so this is not an all-facts-dead test. Concrete decide over all 64 head subsets; no conclusion disjunct.
21. counting_keeps_cycle_over_worlds: for every iteration, both cycle members survive naive countRun over the withdrawn reduct and old world. Induction uses the actual mutual rules; it is not just the zero-iteration identity. Coupled with #20's exact rejection, this refutes counting as world maintenance. No disjunct.

Known scope: finite reference analyzer, exponential enumeration, exact when completed; no theorem of a universal sufficient round budget, no incremental dataflow implementation, no extension of the one-level hole-support closure to recursive holes. Conflict is a diagnostic about supplied evidence (or one encountered evidence world), not a claim that the proposal was admitted. No policy choice or foreign-layer action needs Ember; ROOT must supply the independent theorem reader before landing.

