## Independent statement and disjunct read
Read the actual statements and their definitions/proofs, not only the author's self-read. All 21 conclusions have no Or escape branch. For each iff I checked both directions, and for each conjunction every conjunct is required. Existential results name concrete checked output, not an unrestricted collision witness.
1. derives_head: Derives is an independent finite derivation; the head-membership result follows structurally from reduct membership, not an assumed head-membership field. Empty-body rules inhabit the premise; arbitrary body-only atoms do not.
2. closed_complete: closure and derivability jointly imply computed membership. An unfinished fact at zero rounds refutes dropping closure; a closed empty program refutes inferring arbitrary membership from closure alone.
3. check_iff_stable: compares Boolean iteration/bidirectional inclusion to inductive Derives. Saturation does not force either side true: the union of the two alternatives has a closed empty reduct but is unstable. Both directions are substantive.
4. check_decides: completed Boolean b is not assumed true; stable status exactly tracks it. Completed false is inhabited by the union, and none is excluded explicitly.
5. unfounded_excluded: S has an actual member hx, and rule support is restricted to reduct rules. A grounded fact would falsify hr, so the statement does not exclude actual facts. The cycle supplies a nonempty useful instance.
6. collect_checked: completion of all input candidates, including rejected ones, is required; the Bool witness contains a check equation and cannot be arbitrarily chosen. Empty-input base does not erase nonempty instances.
7. collect_mem: membership is equivalent to input membership AND a successful check. Neither factor suffices alone; rejecting the union and omitting an accepted singleton from the inputs demonstrate the distinction.
8. analyze_exact: completed enumeration AND independent stable semantics characterize membership. Does not infer absence from a partial search; both directions use the completion premise.
9. mem_subsets_iff: computed list enumeration equals structural Sublist, not the same predicate renamed. Neither direction is a conclusion disjunct; [1] under [0,1] and [2] under [0,1] give positive/negative instances.
10. analyze_sublist_exact: structural canonical-world coverage plus Stable; a useful consumer corollary of 8 and 9. No new assumption on a landed theorem.
11. alternatives_sound: report input is arbitrary, so the five conjunctions (two Stable, two evidence memberships, unequal lists) are real guarantees. It does not prove the caller's numeric atoms logically incompatible; that interpretation is explicitly documented. Canonical enumeration prevents two orders of the same set being the returned pair.
12. noJustification_sound: ws is tied to actual completed analysis, ws is nonempty, and both query atoms are absent in every result. The neither-token experiment supplies ws=[[]]; absence cannot be discharged by choosing zero worlds.
13. Experiment.two_rule_worlds: concrete decide checks exact enumeration and both accepted operands. Three required equations, no fabricated witness or tag-only comparison.
14. admissible_not_union_closed: two actual accepted operands and rejection of their concrete union. The acceptance conjuncts prevent rejection of a non-world operand from proving nonclosure.
15. union_not_stable: semantic negation through check_decides for that same union; Stable uses Derives, not check by definition.
16. withdraw_and_reassert: a fixed five-revision session computes exact alternatives at each step via retained rules and real Edit.apply. Restoring applicability exercises the same versioned token.
17. reissue_does_not_restore_rule: new token live, old token dead, old rule still disabled; the three conjuncts rule out the degenerate all-tokens-dead explanation.
18. four_reports: all four distinct analyzer outputs computed on explicit inputs, including zero-fuel unfinished. This tests report execution, not inequality of constructors by hand.
19. no_world_is_distinct: odd negative loop, empty stable world, and one supported side yield three different computed outcomes. Prevents model absence being conflated with evidence absence.
20. cycle_loses_grounding_over_worlds: exact world sets over a withdraw/restore session plus rejection of the obsolete world. Independent fact 5 and consequence 6 persist, so loss of everything is insufficient.
21. counting_keeps_cycle_over_worlds: every n, including successors, retains both mutually supporting atoms in the withdrawn reduct. The induction uses the actual mutual rules; paired with 20 it distinguishes naive counting from grounded analysis.

2026-10-20 VERDICT: LAND. No Lean fixes required. Definition module has only data/definitions/instances; Stable lives in the proof module (C3). Experiments are real kernel decide computations over explicit programs, worlds and sessions; counting's universal result is an induction. The five mutations really bypass defaults, token applicability, grounding, reverse inclusion and completion; every mutant module builds and then the probe is rejected. Whole outputs and error/unbound/No-such-file/Traceback scan contain only the expected decide failures, with exact path/line evidence already listed in CX-P3.report.md. Independent scoped lake --rehash build succeeded (7 warm jobs), followed by fresh elaboration of BOTH source files with -DmaxHeartbeats=200000, 6G/two threads: exit 0, no diagnostics. Logs: /tank/dregg-build/nanodregg/logs/CX-READER-P3-build.log and CX-READER-P3-elaborate.log. No hypotheses added; no landed signatures edited; no pause item identified. Preparing the source gates and landing through scripts/commit.
